# nmcli — real-world examples

## Show devices and connections

```sh
nmcli dev status
nmcli con show
nmcli c s              # short form
```

## Add a DHCP ethernet connection

```sh
nmcli con add type ethernet con-name Myhome1 ifname enp0s3
```

## Add a static IP connection

```sh
nmcli con add type ethernet con-name static2 ifname enp0s3 \
  ip4 192.168.1.50/24 gw4 192.168.1.1
nmcli con mod static2 ipv4.dns "8.8.8.8 8.8.4.4"
```

## Switch between connections

```sh
nmcli con down Myoffice1 ; nmcli con up static1
nmcli con down static1 ; nmcli con up static2
nmcli con mod static2 connection.autoconnect no
```

## Change DNS on an existing connection

```sh
nmcli -f ipv4.dns con show "System eth0"
sudo nmcli con mod "System eth0" ipv4.dns "10.0.0.2"
sudo nmcli con up "System eth0"
cat /etc/resolv.conf
host www.google.com
```

## Homelab: pin a static address on the Tumbleweed box

```sh
sudo nmcli con add type ethernet con-name homelab-static ifname eth0 \
  ip4 192.168.1.42/24 gw4 192.168.1.1
sudo nmcli con mod homelab-static ipv4.dns "192.168.1.1"
sudo nmcli con up homelab-static
```

| Command            | What it does                       |
| ------------------ | ---------------------------------- |
| nmcli dev status   | list devices and their state       |
| nmcli con show     | list connections                   |
| nmcli con add      | create a connection                |
| nmcli con mod      | change connection settings         |
| nmcli con up/down  | activate / deactivate a connection |
